WEBVTT

00:07.940 --> 00:11.020
<i>One bronze piece for a job payment, huh?</i>

00:11.540 --> 00:13.500
<i>That basically means working for free,</i>

00:13.500 --> 00:16.110
<i>but a surprising amount of 
adventurers will take it.</i>

00:16.110 --> 00:18.790
<i>We're not doing this just for the money.</i>

00:18.790 --> 00:21.480
<i>Sometimes, we'll take jobs to help people.</i>

00:21.880 --> 00:26.390
<i>Well, the guild wouldn't 
take a job request like</i>

00:26.410 --> 00:28.800
<i>"Defeat the Legendary Lord of the Lake."</i>

00:29.320 --> 00:31.580
Any jobs catch your eye?

00:31.820 --> 00:33.410
Sheila?

00:33.410 --> 00:34.770
Don't worry.

00:34.770 --> 00:37.670
I'm not going into the Labyrinth 
for a while, just like I promised.

00:37.670 --> 00:43.060
Oh, no... I thought I could help 
if you were looking for a quick job.

00:43.380 --> 00:44.590
Great.

00:44.590 --> 00:47.560
Is nobody going to take this quest?

00:47.560 --> 00:51.320
Oh, the one with the single
bronze piece reward?

00:51.320 --> 00:56.200
It's a guild tradition, so everyone 
at least thinks about it.

00:56.200 --> 00:58.200
But it's pretty difficult...

00:58.200 --> 01:00.540
Gathering a Dragonblood Flower...

01:00.540 --> 01:01.790
Yeah.

01:01.790 --> 01:05.410
They only bloom next to poisonous swamps.

01:05.410 --> 01:07.950
The story about them is 
so wonderful, though...

01:07.950 --> 01:11.500
A dragon fell in love with a human woman...

01:11.500 --> 01:16.210
His blood became a bright red flower 
called the Dragonblood Flower.

01:16.860 --> 01:19.110
A rather gruesome story.

01:20.510 --> 01:25.320
Girls who receive that flower 
are said to be loved forever.

01:25.620 --> 01:28.600
Well, I have heard that story.

01:29.050 --> 01:31.820
But for this job, they want 
it as medicine, right?

01:31.820 --> 01:36.060
Yes. It's a job from the 
children at an orphanage.

01:36.060 --> 01:40.450
They say they need the Dragonblood Flower 
to save someone they care about.

01:40.450 --> 01:41.830
I see.

01:43.330 --> 01:45.080
Rentt, are you...

03:19.510 --> 03:23.680
<b>Dragonblood 
Flower</b>

03:19.890 --> 03:21.780
So this is the place, huh?

03:21.780 --> 03:24.210
It's more run-down than I expected.

03:26.870 --> 03:28.170
Oh...

03:29.080 --> 03:30.220
<i>Oh, right.</i>

03:30.480 --> 03:32.650
<i>I might be able to use the fluids 
from that slime to fix it.</i>

03:37.860 --> 03:39.670
<i>Well, that kind of worked...</i>

03:45.710 --> 03:47.430
Coming!

03:48.210 --> 03:52.520
I'm sorry. Headmistress 
Lillian isn't in right now.

03:52.520 --> 03:55.250
You'll have to come back another time...

03:56.100 --> 03:59.810
I'm an adventurer. I took 
the job at the guild.

03:59.810 --> 04:03.730
Oh, I was sure you were a debt collector.

04:03.730 --> 04:05.110
I see.

04:05.110 --> 04:07.030
Please, come in.

04:07.030 --> 04:08.840
It's a little cramped, but...

04:08.840 --> 04:10.060
Thank you.

04:15.270 --> 04:17.650
Everyone, be on your best behavior.

04:17.650 --> 04:19.930
He's an adventurer.

04:20.740 --> 04:22.240
Wow, you're an adventurer?

04:23.060 --> 04:24.430
Is that sword real?

04:24.430 --> 04:25.830
Are you strong?

04:25.830 --> 04:27.650
Why are you dressed so weird?

04:27.650 --> 04:32.620
Hey! I told you all that adventurers 
are dangerous barbarians,

04:32.620 --> 04:34.950
so you needed to stay away from them!

04:34.950 --> 04:36.610
Sorry...

04:37.430 --> 04:39.280
Um, I'm sorry...

04:39.280 --> 04:41.860
I didn't mean you specifically.

04:41.860 --> 04:44.380
No, it actually makes me feel better.

04:45.350 --> 04:48.690
Adventurers can be the rowdy sort.

04:48.690 --> 04:50.780
It's only natural to be cautious.

04:53.050 --> 04:54.350
Listen, everyone.

04:54.350 --> 04:58.370
You need to stay away from 
weird-looking adults.

04:58.370 --> 05:00.240
Okay.

05:01.370 --> 05:03.380
They seem like good kids.

05:03.380 --> 05:05.380
I apologize.

05:05.380 --> 05:07.970
It can be dangerous to be too trusting,

05:07.970 --> 05:11.030
but it just shows they've 
had a happy upbringing.

05:11.030 --> 05:15.140
Yes! Headmistress Lillian is a great woman!

05:15.140 --> 05:18.340
I mean, a wonderful lady!

05:18.340 --> 05:20.520
You can speak normally around me.

05:20.520 --> 05:22.180
But...

05:22.180 --> 05:25.160
You should be more polite 
around adults, yes.

05:25.160 --> 05:27.390
But I don't mind.

05:27.390 --> 05:29.300
You won't get mad later?

05:29.300 --> 05:30.270
Of course not.

05:30.710 --> 05:32.780
My name is Rentt Vivie.

05:32.780 --> 05:34.470
I'm a Bronze-class adventurer.

05:34.470 --> 05:40.480
Bronze? I was sure the best 
we'd get was an Iron-class.

05:40.480 --> 05:42.150
You know a lot about us.

05:42.150 --> 05:43.580
Did you make the request?

05:43.580 --> 05:46.730
Yes. My name is Alize.

05:47.040 --> 05:50.470
Then Alize, let's talk about the job.

05:50.470 --> 05:53.740
Dragonblood Flowers aren't easy to get.

05:54.740 --> 05:56.410
I know.

05:56.410 --> 05:58.860
You can barely find them at any stores.

05:58.860 --> 06:01.190
And even if you do, they're very expensive.

06:01.190 --> 06:03.470
But you need one anyway.

06:03.470 --> 06:04.390
Yes.

06:04.940 --> 06:07.440
I want to know more.

06:07.440 --> 06:10.710
All right. But you'll need to keep our secret.

06:11.360 --> 06:12.720
Secret?

06:13.920 --> 06:17.340
I'm sorry I can't get out 
of bed to welcome you.

06:17.340 --> 06:23.990
My name is Lillian June. I'm a priestess 
of the Eastern Sky Church.

06:23.990 --> 06:26.660
I'm Rentt Vivie. An adventurer.

06:27.070 --> 06:31.070
I'm so glad you're helping to clean 
out the orphanage's basement,

06:31.070 --> 06:33.150
even though we can only 
pay such a small amount.

06:33.150 --> 06:35.480
Thank you, so much.

06:35.480 --> 06:37.530
Well, it's a good change of pace.

06:37.860 --> 06:41.300
The basement is small, but 
monsters do appear down there,

06:41.300 --> 06:43.890
so I can't have the children doing it.

06:44.410 --> 06:46.790
Rest, Headmistress!

06:46.790 --> 06:49.520
I'll tell him the rest.

06:50.230 --> 06:52.000
Thank you, Alize.

06:56.120 --> 07:00.710
Her disease is called Malaccumula.

07:01.260 --> 07:03.310
Malaccumula?

07:03.310 --> 07:04.270
Yes.

07:04.270 --> 07:07.330
She's a divinity user.

07:07.330 --> 07:10.460
But if your divinity isn't strong,

07:10.460 --> 07:15.280
each time you use it there's a reaction that 
causes evil energy to accumulate in the body.

07:15.730 --> 07:19.460
It won't kill her anytime soon, but...

07:19.460 --> 07:21.640
I didn't know there was such a thing.

07:21.640 --> 07:25.750
We had a healer look at 
her, so it has to be that.

07:25.750 --> 07:31.420
The only way to heal it is with the blood 
of a holy maiden, or a special medicine.

07:31.420 --> 07:32.960
I see.

07:33.220 --> 07:38.370
And you need the Dragonblood Flower 
to make this special medicine?

07:38.370 --> 07:39.470
Yes.

07:39.790 --> 07:42.880
She doesn't know what her 
disease is, does she?

07:42.880 --> 07:43.920
She doesn't.

07:43.920 --> 07:50.270
If she knew, she'd have another 
priestess take over the orphanage.

07:50.800 --> 07:53.560
And then she'd leave the orphanage,

07:53.560 --> 07:57.010
and accept the disease 
as the will of heaven...

08:00.550 --> 08:04.370
Well, we'll need to get the Dragonblood 
Flower before that happens, then.

08:05.600 --> 08:08.550
I was sure nobody would take the job...

08:08.550 --> 08:09.980
You were?

08:09.980 --> 08:15.520
But if that happened, I was going to become 
an adventurer and go get it myself!

08:16.540 --> 08:19.370
I've got a little bit of mana, you know.

08:19.870 --> 08:23.180
But you don't have time to learn 
how to be an adventurer...

08:24.830 --> 08:27.640
I can really ask you to do it?

08:27.950 --> 08:30.730
Yeah. I'll get it for you. I promise.

08:32.040 --> 08:33.950
Thank you, Rentt!

08:33.950 --> 08:35.770
But first...

08:36.510 --> 08:39.160
I'll clean up that basement.

08:52.460 --> 08:54.670
You don't need to follow me.

08:54.670 --> 08:57.570
No, you're fighting monsters, right?

08:57.570 --> 09:00.900
I don't think it's that fun to watch, but...

09:01.200 --> 09:04.050
You can't use a sword 
in a room this cramped.

09:05.060 --> 09:07.070
Take it, just in case.

09:07.070 --> 09:08.460
Okay.

09:10.470 --> 09:12.700
Looks like they're here.

09:12.700 --> 09:13.620
Huh? Really?

09:17.990 --> 09:20.730
Pretty big, for a puchi suri.

09:38.560 --> 09:39.670
What?

09:44.260 --> 09:46.150
<i>It changed color?</i>

09:46.470 --> 09:47.900
<i>This feeling...</i>

09:47.900 --> 09:48.930
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

09:49.850 --> 09:51.910
Spin around three times in a circle.

10:00.150 --> 10:05.290
Rentt, what's that chubby little 
black rat on your shoulder?

10:05.690 --> 10:08.420
It joined my party in the 
orphanage's basement.

10:09.020 --> 10:10.710
You're skipping a lot there.

10:12.940 --> 10:17.300
Vampires have the power to 
make and control familiars.

10:17.300 --> 10:19.730
I didn't know you could do 
the same thing, though.

10:19.730 --> 10:21.340
I guess I can.

10:21.340 --> 10:24.600
True. I hadn't actually done any 
experiments to see what would happen

10:24.600 --> 10:26.800
if I gave your blood to 
another creature yet.

10:27.340 --> 10:28.950
Can I keep him?

10:28.950 --> 10:30.680
Sure, if you want.

10:30.680 --> 10:33.790
We've already got an undead living here.

10:33.790 --> 10:37.580
A rat or two won't change a thing.

10:38.210 --> 10:40.330
He'll have to pay rent, though.

10:41.290 --> 10:42.530
Rent?

10:42.530 --> 10:45.160
I want samples of his blood and hair.

10:45.160 --> 10:46.880
There's a lot I want to try.

10:48.610 --> 10:51.370
And I also want to do an ecology study.

10:51.650 --> 10:53.710
What do you eat?

10:54.330 --> 10:55.850
Hey!

10:55.850 --> 10:59.080
I see. Just like your dad, then.

10:59.080 --> 11:02.640
I guess my blood is quite popular.

11:02.640 --> 11:05.460
Hey, what are you going to call him?

11:05.460 --> 11:07.720
Blackie, 'cause he's black.

11:08.520 --> 11:10.780
You could put a little more thought into it.

11:10.780 --> 11:13.770
Fine. I'll name him.

11:13.770 --> 11:15.800
How about "Edel"?

11:17.070 --> 11:18.440
An excellent name, yes?

11:18.440 --> 11:21.440
It means "Noble One" in the ancient tongue.

11:21.750 --> 11:25.400
I heard you were the leader 
of the other puchi suri.

11:25.400 --> 11:27.500
He seems satisfied.

11:27.500 --> 11:29.810
You can communicate with him?

11:29.810 --> 11:33.170
I can't speak his language, but I 
can kinda tell what he's thinking.

11:33.170 --> 11:36.160
From now on, then, you're Edel.

11:36.160 --> 11:38.630
And I'm the one who named you.

11:39.640 --> 11:42.260
Hey, I'm your master, okay?

11:48.640 --> 11:53.490
<i>Since I became an undead, I stopped 
needing sleep almost entirely.</i>

11:53.490 --> 11:56.110
<i>I thought about never leaving the labyrinth,</i>

11:56.520 --> 12:00.940
<i>but people would get suspicious of an 
adventurer that never took any rest.</i>

12:03.200 --> 12:05.530
<i>These hours are so incredibly boring...</i>

12:09.210 --> 12:10.510
Come in.

12:13.050 --> 12:15.780
You're leaving early in the morning, right?

12:15.780 --> 12:18.380
Why not fill your belly, first?

12:21.270 --> 12:23.750
I wonder if it's a sign it'll snow today...

12:23.750 --> 12:25.590
Don't be ridiculous.

12:25.930 --> 12:28.540
I can cook too, you know.

12:28.540 --> 12:30.030
I do know.

12:30.030 --> 12:34.980
Then you know how dangerous the 
Tarasque Swamp is too, then.

12:34.980 --> 12:37.250
How did you know where I'm going?

12:37.930 --> 12:40.190
Well, I guess you would.

12:40.190 --> 12:41.760
Of course I do.

12:41.760 --> 12:45.810
That's the only swamp around here where 
you can find a Dragonblood Flower.

12:45.810 --> 12:46.660
Yeah.

12:47.130 --> 12:48.880
Are you going alone?

12:48.880 --> 12:52.160
If I go alone, I won't have 
to worry about the poison.

12:52.160 --> 12:54.810
There's Tarasque there. A type of wyvern.

12:54.810 --> 12:57.340
Even Bronze-class adventurers 
would take a party to go there.

12:57.340 --> 12:58.870
I'm not going to fight.

12:58.870 --> 13:00.210
What?

13:00.490 --> 13:02.650
I bought this for cheap at a roadside stall.

13:02.650 --> 13:04.460
Holy water?

13:04.460 --> 13:10.030
Yes, they do say you can keep Tarasque 
away by using holy water, but...

13:10.030 --> 13:12.090
It doesn't always work.

13:12.090 --> 13:14.480
Well, it'll work out.

13:15.910 --> 13:17.150
Listen, you...

13:17.150 --> 13:19.160
It would be a waste to let this get cold.

13:19.160 --> 13:20.860
I'll eat it while it's still hot.

13:25.950 --> 13:27.270
Is it good?

13:27.270 --> 13:28.470
Yeah.

13:28.470 --> 13:32.740
I haven't enjoyed normal food 
this much in a long time.

13:33.260 --> 13:36.360
I put a drop of my blood in it.

13:36.630 --> 13:38.050
So that's why...

13:39.780 --> 13:41.130
Like it?

13:41.510 --> 13:43.010
Yeah.

13:43.010 --> 13:46.030
I'll make you another 
batch when you get back.

13:56.200 --> 13:58.830
We're here, mister.

13:58.830 --> 13:59.950
Thanks.

14:05.370 --> 14:07.870
This is as far as I can take you.

14:07.870 --> 14:10.660
I'll come and get you this evening.

14:10.660 --> 14:11.800
Thanks.

14:16.460 --> 14:19.080
The poison doesn't bother you?

14:20.740 --> 14:24.510
<i>Well, I can purify it with 
my divinity if I have to.</i>

14:24.510 --> 14:25.790
<i>It'll be fine.</i>

14:26.980 --> 14:28.700
<i>The Tarasque Swamp.</i>

14:28.700 --> 14:32.620
<i>It has another name, but nobody uses it.</i>

14:33.180 --> 14:37.170
<i>There are rare animals and plants 
that can only be found here,</i>

14:37.170 --> 14:39.740
<i>so it's been made at least passable.</i>

14:40.440 --> 14:44.850
<i>Nobody wants to stick their 
foot into a poison swamp.</i>

14:51.950 --> 14:56.260
<i>Monsters found in the wild are stronger 
than the ones in the labyrinth.</i>

14:56.260 --> 15:00.880
<i>That's because they use weapons, 
or know how to fight in groups.</i>

15:00.880 --> 15:03.500
<i>They're tough opponents, but 
now I'm strong enough to...</i>

15:10.970 --> 15:13.060
<i>Easily defeat a few goblins.</i>

15:16.360 --> 15:18.860
Next time, you work, too.

15:19.800 --> 15:24.490
You don't think that you're the master 
in this relationship, do you?

15:25.430 --> 15:26.990
Sheesh...

15:29.560 --> 15:33.140
<i>It sure is handy being undead, though!</i>

15:33.140 --> 15:34.920
<i>I have poison resistance, for one thing.</i>

15:34.920 --> 15:36.620
<i>If I could just do something 
about my appearance,</i>

15:36.620 --> 15:39.030
<i>I might be willing to 
stay like this forever!</i>

15:39.460 --> 15:41.750
<i>I could probably never get married, though.</i>

15:45.910 --> 15:48.650
<i>He jumped and let me fall, the bastard.</i>

15:52.930 --> 15:55.190
<i>I've got some horrible luck today.</i>

16:03.140 --> 16:04.990
<i>I can't let my guard down for a moment.</i>

16:13.110 --> 16:17.190
<i>Are all vampire familiars like this?</i>

16:18.880 --> 16:20.740
Thank you for the meal.

16:20.740 --> 16:22.700
It was delicious.

16:22.700 --> 16:24.100
You liked it?

16:24.100 --> 16:26.360
Rentt certainly enjoyed it.

16:26.360 --> 16:28.920
But isn't Rentt...

16:29.340 --> 16:32.640
I mixed my blood in with it.

16:33.670 --> 16:36.660
Don't worry. Just in his portion.

16:38.470 --> 16:43.440
Anyway, I'm surprised the guild's already 
aware of what happened at Tottsu village.

16:43.440 --> 16:46.460
We had to help transport the criminals.

16:46.460 --> 16:51.320
The villagers were very grateful 
to the adventurer who helped them.

16:51.710 --> 16:56.310
They refused to say his name no matter 
how many times we asked, though.

16:56.310 --> 16:58.700
So you came to talk to him directly?

16:59.320 --> 17:02.030
I assume he wouldn't want to 
talk about it at the guild...

17:02.030 --> 17:06.190
Knowing Rentt, he assumed that even 
if he was the hero of that story,

17:06.190 --> 17:10.330
any association of him and the word "kidnapping"
would just make people more suspicious.

17:11.050 --> 17:14.230
He can sometimes do things 
you'd never expect him to,

17:14.230 --> 17:16.560
but he does know how to 
think things through.

17:17.280 --> 17:19.860
You know him well.

17:19.860 --> 17:22.570
I've known him a long time, after all.

17:22.570 --> 17:25.790
Then do you know...?

17:25.790 --> 17:26.720
Know what?

17:28.640 --> 17:32.850
Why becoming a Mythril-class 
adventurer is so important to him.

17:37.230 --> 17:38.380
Nope.

17:39.380 --> 17:42.370
I've never heard him talk 
about that, actually.

17:42.370 --> 17:44.510
You haven't?

17:44.510 --> 17:49.370
I've been told that adventurers don't 
ask each other about their pasts.

17:49.370 --> 17:52.090
Part of it is that I don't 
want to get too nosy, but...

17:52.450 --> 17:55.050
you know how he is.

17:55.050 --> 17:57.510
You don't worry?

17:57.510 --> 18:01.640
Even with the job he's on today... 
he might have to fight a Tarasque.

18:01.940 --> 18:03.990
What a strange thing to say.

18:03.990 --> 18:07.030
The guild puts a lot of work into 
making sure adventurers only take jobs

18:07.030 --> 18:08.890
appropriate for their strength, right?

18:08.890 --> 18:14.590
Of course. We judged him strong enough 
for the task before giving it to him.

18:14.590 --> 18:16.590
Then what's the problem?

18:17.780 --> 18:21.620
I'll defer to the opinion of 
our talented guild staff.

18:22.790 --> 18:24.190
And what's more...

18:24.590 --> 18:27.020
Even if something does happen...

18:27.020 --> 18:30.910
an adventurer always finds a way, right?

18:32.380 --> 18:36.260
<i>Damn it! I should've known that 
holy water was too cheap to work!</i>

18:38.480 --> 18:39.890
<i>A dead end...</i>

18:43.650 --> 18:44.980
<i>I'll have to fight, huh?</i>

18:56.360 --> 18:58.210
Too bad.

18:58.210 --> 18:59.820
Poison won't work on me.

19:01.360 --> 19:05.210
<i>I don't think I can defeat you 
with just my mana, either.</i>

19:17.210 --> 19:19.160
<i>It didn't work, huh?</i>

19:21.680 --> 19:23.330
<i>That's not good.</i>

19:24.580 --> 19:25.520
Edel!

19:29.750 --> 19:33.120
Is that divinity? Is he using my power?

19:37.230 --> 19:38.340
Edel!

19:48.760 --> 19:49.940
Are you okay?

19:51.060 --> 19:53.840
Don't use my divinity without my okay.

19:53.840 --> 19:56.700
That did give me a good hint, though.

20:34.540 --> 20:38.380
I see. A Tarasque's 
weakness is divinity.

20:39.530 --> 20:42.460
Yeah. You helped, too.

20:43.550 --> 20:48.860
But I can't field dress it here. 
Not when it's this big...

20:56.150 --> 20:57.400
There we go.

21:03.620 --> 21:07.070
<i>I've got bad luck. That's 
one thing I'm sure of.</i>

21:07.500 --> 21:10.940
<i>I was pretty sure I'd have 
to fight a Tarasque.</i>

21:11.390 --> 21:15.210
<i>Thanks to him, though,
I've learned how to do it.</i>

21:16.470 --> 21:19.040
<i>I can find a lot of rare materials here, too.</i>

21:19.040 --> 21:20.500
<i>I'll come back soon.</i>

21:31.310 --> 21:34.290
<i>Are these all Dragonblood flowers?</i>

21:35.410 --> 21:39.190
<i>Their power is purifying this whole area.</i>

21:41.800 --> 21:44.480
<i>It's safe to take a few more 
than I came for, I'm sure.</i>

21:53.220 --> 21:57.580
Oh my. I'm surprised to 
see someone else here.

23:35.560 --> 23:39.850
A Strange Man and a Strange Job
